hadiths[65]{hadithnumber,text}:
"617","Abu Dharr narrated:\I came to the Messenger of Allah while he was sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah.\"" He said: \""He saw me approaching and he said: 'They are lost on the Day of Judgment! By the Lord of the Ka'bah!'\"" He said: \""I said t myself: Woe is me! Perhaps something has been revealed about me!'\"" He said: \""So I said: 'Who are they"""""
"618","Abu Hurairah narrated :that the Prophet said: \When you pay the Zakat you have fulfilled what is required of you"""""
"619","Anas narrated:\We used to hope that an intelligent Bedouin would show up to question the Prophet while we were with him. So one while we were with him"""""
"620","Ali narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \I have exempted charity on horses and slaves. So bring charity for silver"""""
"621","Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Baghdadi, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi, and Muhammad ibn Kamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, the meaning being one, saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the book of zakah but did not send it out to his workers until he passed away. He kept it with his sword. When he passed away, Abu Bakr acted upon it until he passed away, and Umar until he passed away. In it was: ""In five camels, a sheep; in ten, two sheep; in fifteen, three sheep; in twenty, four sheep; in twenty-five, a bint makhad up to thirty-five; if they increase, then a bint labun up to forty-five; if they increase, then a hiqqah up to sixty; if they increase, then a jadh'ah up to seventy-five; if they increase, then two bint labun up to ninety; if they increase, then two hiqqah up to one hundred and twenty; if they exceed one hundred and twenty, then in every fifty a hiqqah, and in every forty a bint labun. In sheep: in every forty sheep a sheep up to one hundred and twenty; if they increase, then two sheep up to two hundred; if they increase, then three sheep up to three hundred sheep; if they exceed three hundred sheep, then in every hundred sheep a sheep. Then there is nothing in it until they reach four hundred. No combining between separate flocks and no separating combined flocks for fear of zakah. And what belongs to two partners, they settle between them equally. No decrepit animal is taken in zakah, nor one with a defect."" Al-Zuhri said: When the collector comes, he divides the sheep into thirds: a third choice, a third medium, a third poor, and the collector takes from the medium. Al-Zuhri did not mention cattle. In this chapter there are narrations from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Bahz ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather, Abu Dharr, and Anas. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Ibn Umar is hasan. The practice is upon this hadith according to the generality of the jurists. Yunus ibn Yazid and others narrated from al-Zuhri from Salim this hadith and did not raise it; only Sufyan ibn Husayn raised it."
"622","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that :the Prophet said: \A Tabi or a Tabi'ah (is due) on thirty cows"""""
"623","Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated:\The Prophet sent me to Yemen and ordered me to collect a Tabi or a Tabi'ah on every thirty cows"""""
"624","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I asked Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allah, \Do you recall anything from 'Abd Allah?\"" He replied"
"625","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah sent Mu'adh to Yemen and said to him: \You are going to a people from the People of the Book"""""
"626","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :the Prophet said: \There is no charity due on less than five camels"""""
"627","(Another chain of narration that) Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :the Prophet said (similar t Hadith no)"
"628","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \There is no charity due from a Muslim for his horse nor his slave"""""
"629","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \A Ziqq is due for every ten Ziqq of honey"""""
"630","Ubaidulah bin Umar narrated that :Nafi said: \Umar bin Adbul-Aziz asked me about charity due on honey"""""
"631","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever acquired wealth"""""
"632","Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with both of them), who said:\n\n\Whoever acquires wealth"
"633","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Two Qiblahs in one land are of no benefit"""""
"634","Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Jarīr narrated to us, from Qābūs, through this chain of transmission, something similar to it. In this chapter, there are narrations from Saʿīd ibn Zayd and the grandfather of Ḥarb ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Thaqafī. Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: The ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās has also been narrated from Qābūs ibn Abī Ẓabyān, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a mursal form. The practice according to the generality of the scholars is that when a Christian embraces Islam, the jizyah (poll tax) upon his person is waived. The statement of the Prophet ﷺ, “There are no ʿushūr (taxes) upon the Muslims,” refers specifically to the jizyah upon the person. The ḥadīth itself clarifies this, as he ﷺ said, “Indeed, the ʿushūr are upon the Jews and the Christians, and there are no ʿushūr upon the Muslims.”"
"635","Amr bin Al-Harith bin Al-Mustaliq narrated from the nephew of Zainab"
"636","Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān, who narrated from Abū Dāwūd, from Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, who said: \I heard Abū Wāʾil narrating from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith"
"637","Narrated by Qutaybah, narrated to us Ibn Luhay'ah, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that two women came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with gold bracelets in their hands. He asked them: \Do you pay its zakah?\"" They replied: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then asked them: \""Would you like Allah to adorn you with bracelets of fire?\"" They replied: \""No.\"" He then said: \""Then pay its zakah.\"" Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] commented: This hadith has also been narrated by Al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabah from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb in a similar manner. However"
"638","Eisa bin Talhah narrated that :Mu'adh had written to the Prophet to ask him about greens - which is \herbs\"" - so he (pbuh) said"""""
"639","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \For what is watered by the heavens and steams"""""
"640","Salim narrated from his father that :the Messenger of Allah instituted the Ushr of what was watered by the heavens and steams"
"641","Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, addressed the people and said: “Beware! Whoever is the guardian of an orphan who possesses wealth, let him trade with it and not leave it, lest it be consumed by ṣadaqah (i.e., zakāh).”\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This ḥadīth has been narrated only from this chain, and there is discussion regarding its isnād, because al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ is considered weak in ḥadīth. Some have narrated this ḥadīth from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, attributing it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and he mentioned this ḥadīth.\n\nThe scholars have differed on this matter. A number of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, held that zakāh is due on the wealth of an orphan. Among them were ʿUmar, ʿAlī, ʿĀʾishah, and Ibn ʿUmar. This is also the view of Mālik, al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq.\n\nAnother group of scholars held that there is no zakāh on the wealth of an orphan. This is the view of Sufyān al-Thawrī and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak.\n\nʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is the son of Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, and Shuʿayb heard from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr.\n\nYaḥyā ibn Saʿīd spoke critically of the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and said: “In our view, it is weak.” Those who deemed him weak did so because he narrated from the scroll of his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. However, the majority of the ḥadīth scholars rely upon the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and consider it acceptable, among them Aḥmad, Isḥāq, and others."
"642","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \The injuries caused by the animal are without liability"""""
"643","Abdur-Rahman bin Mas'ud bin Niyar said:\Sahl bin Abi Hathmah came to a gathering of ours"""""
"644","Attab bin Asid narrated that :the Prophet said about Zakat on grapevines: \They are to be assessed just as the date-palm is assessed. Then its Zakat is paid in raisins just as the Zakat for the date-palm is paid in dried dates"""""
"645","Rafi bin Khadij narrated:\I herd the Messenger of Allah saying: 'The one who works in collecting charity in truth is like the one who fights in the cause of Allah until he returns"""""
"646","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \The one who commits transgression with charity is like the one who does not pay it"""""
"647","Jarir narrated that :the Prophet said: \When the charity collector comes to you"""""
"648","Jarir narrated :similar (narration to no. 647 with a different chain) from the Prophet"
"649","Awn bin Abi Jubaitah narrated from his father:\The charity collector of the Prophet came to us. So he took the charity from our rich to our poor. I was a orphan boy"""""
"650","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever begs from the people while he has what he needs"""""
"651","Mahmud bin Ghaydin narrated to us:Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated this Hadith to us from Hakim bin Jubair. So Abdullah bin Uthman, the companion of Shu'bah said to him (Sufyan): ""If only someone besides Hakim had narrated this (Hadith)."" Sufyan said to him, ""So what is with Hakim; Shu'bah would not narrate from him?"" He said: ""Yes."" So Sufyan said: ""I heard Zubaid narrating this from Muhammad bin Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid"
"652","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that :the Prophet said: \Charity is not lawful for the rich nor for the physically fit"""""
"653","Hubshi bin Junadah As-Saluli narrated:""During the Farewell Hajj, while the Messener of allah was standing at Arafat, a Bedouin came to him begging while pulling on the edge of his Rida. He gave him something and he left. With that, begging was made unlawful, so the Messenger of Allah said: 'Begging is not lawful for the rich nor for the physically fit, except for the one who is severely poor or in perilous debt. And whoever begs the people (merely) to increase his wealth, then on the Day of Judgment (the wealth he begged for) will be lacerations on his face and heated coals from Hell will be provided for him to eat. Whoever wishes, let him take a little, and whoever wishes, then let him take a lot"
"654","Narrator mentioned in hadith:There is another chain with a similar narration"
"655","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:\During the time of the Messenger of Allah"""""
"656","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim and Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i al-Sadusi narrated to us, they both said: Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when something was brought to him, he would ask: \Is it charity (sadaqah) or a gift (hadiyyah)?\"" If they said it was charity"
"657","Abu Rafi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah sent a man from Banu Makhzun to collect charity"
"658","Qutaybah narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us — from ʿĀsim al-Aḥwal — from Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn — from al-Rabāb — from her paternal uncle, Salmān ibn ʿĀmir, who traced it back to the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n> \When one of you breaks his fast"
"659","It was narrated to us by Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maddūyah, who reported from al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir, from Sharīk, from Abū Ḥamzah, from al-Shaʿbī, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, who said:\n\n\I asked — or the Prophet ﷺ was asked — about zakāh. He ﷺ said: 'Indeed"
"660","Fatimah bint Qais narrated that :the Prophet said: \Indeed there is a duty on wealth aside from Zakat"""""
"661","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \None gives charity from Tayyib - and Allah does not accept but Tayyib - but that Ar-Rahman accepts it with His Right (Hand). Even if it is a date"""""
"662","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-‘Ala’ narrated to us; Waki’ narrated to us; ‘Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us; al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us; he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Verily, Allah accepts charity and takes it with His Right Hand, then He nurtures it for one of you just as one of you nurtures his foal, until the morsel becomes like (the mountain of) Uhud."" And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: (And He is the One Who accepts repentance from His servants) and takes the charities (Allah destroys usury and gives increase for charities). Abu ‘Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. And it has been narrated from ‘A’ishah from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly. And more than one of the people of knowledge said concerning this hadith and similar narrations regarding the Attributes and the Descent of the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, every night to the lowest heaven: They said the narrations are established in this regard, we believe in them, we do not imagine (how), nor do we say ""How?"" Thus it was narrated from Malik, Sufyan ibn ‘Uyaynah, and ‘Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak that they said concerning these hadiths: ""Pass them on as they came, without asking 'How'."" And this is the saying of the people of knowledge from Ahl al-Sunnah wa al-Jama‘ah. As for the Jahmiyyah, they denied these narrations and said: ""This is anthropomorphism (tashbih)."" And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has mentioned in several places in His Book the Hand, the Hearing, and the Seeing. So the Jahmiyyah interpreted these verses, explaining them contrary to the explanation of the people of knowledge, and they said: ""Allah did not create Adam with His Hand."" And they said the meaning of ""Hand"" here is ""Power."" Ishaq ibn Ibrahim said: Anthropomorphism only occurs if one says: ""A Hand like a Hand"" or ""Similar to a Hand"" or ""Hearing like Hearing"" or ""Similar to Hearing."" So if one says ""Hearing like Hearing"" or ""Similar to Hearing,"" this is anthropomorphism. But if one says as Allah the Exalted said: ""Hand,"" ""Hearing,"" ""Seeing,"" and does not say ""How,"" nor ""Like Hearing,"" nor ""Similar to Hearing,"" then this is not anthropomorphism; and it is as Allah the Exalted said in His Book: {There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing}."
"663","Anas narrated that :the Prophet was asked which fast was most virtuous after Ramadan? He said: \Sha'ban in honor of Ramadan\"" He said: \""Which charity is best?\"" He (pbuh) said: \""Charity in Ramadan"""""
"664","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Indeed charity extinguishes the Lord's anger and it protects against the evil death"""""
"665","Abdur-Rahman bin Bujaid narrated from his grandmother; :Umm Bujaid - and she was one of those who gave the pledge to the Prophet - she said to the Messenger of Allah: \There is a needy person who stands outside my door"""""
"666","Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah who said:\The Messenger of Allah gave to me on the Day of Hunain"""""
"667","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father:\I was sitting with the Prophet when a woman came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I gave a slave girl to my mother in charity and she died.' He said: 'Your reward is already established"""""
"668","Ibn Umar narrated that :Umar gave a horse to be used in the cause of Allah. Then he saw it being sold"
"669","Ikrimah narrated from Ibn Abbas that :a man said: \O Messenger of Allah! My mother died"""""
"670","Abu Umamah Al-Bahili said:\During a sermon of his in the year of the Farewell Hajj"""""
"671","Aishah narrated that :the Prophet said: \When a woman gives in charity from her husband's house"""""
"672","Aishah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: \When a woman gives from her husband's home"""""
"673","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:\We would give Zakat Al-Fitr - when the Messenger of Allah was among us - as a Sa of food"""""
"674","Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his grandfather that :the Prophet sent a caller in the roads of Makkah proclaiming \Sadaqatul-Fitr is required upon every Muslim"""""
"675","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Messenger of Allah made Sadaqatul-Fitr an obligation upon the male and female"""""
"676","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Messenger of Allah made Sadaqatul-Fitr of Ramadan an obligation - a Sa of dried dates or a Sa of barley - required upon every free person and slave"""""
"677","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Messenger of Allah would order paying the Zakat before going to the Salat on the day of Fitr"
"678","Ali narrated:\Al-Abbas asked the Messenger of Allah about paying his charity (Zakat) in advance before its time is due (by being in possession for a whole year)"""""
"679","Ali narrated that :the Prophet said to Umar: \We have taken this year's Zakat from Al-Abbas in the previous year"""""
"680","Abu Hurairah narrated that he heard :the Messenger of Allah saying: \For one of you to go out early to gather firewood and carry it on his back so that he can give charity from it and be free of need from the people"""""
"681","Samurah bin Jundub narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Asking is a labor that toils on a man's face"""""
